---
const groups = [
  ["Manner", "How?", "gently, quickly, well, carefully", "She closed the door gently."],
  ["Time", "When?", "now, yesterday, later, soon, tomorrow", "We will meet later."],
  ["Place", "Where?", "here, outside, nearby, upstairs", "Please wait outside."],
  ["Frequency", "How often?", "always, often, sometimes, rarely, never", "He often reads at night."],
  ["Possibility", "How sure?", "perhaps, probably, certainly", "She will probably arrive."]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Adverbs - What they are</h1>
  <p>
    An <strong>adverb</strong> adds information to a sentence. It often tells us more about a verb, and it can also add information to an adjective or another adverb. Ask what the word tells us or changes. Do not decide from the spelling alone.
  </p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-sand">
    <h2>Three jobs</h2>
    <p>She spoke <strong>quietly</strong>. <em>Quietly</em> tells us how she spoke.</p>
    <p>The water was <strong>very</strong> cold. <em>Very</em> makes the adjective <em>cold</em> stronger.</p>
    <p>He ran <strong>really</strong> quickly. <em>Really</em> strengthens the adverb <em>quickly</em>.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>Five meaning groups</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Type</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Question</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Examples</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          groups.map(([type, question, examples, sentence]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{type}</th>
              <td>{question}</td>
              <td>
                {examples}. {sentence}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>A sentence can hold several adverbs. “<strong>Yesterday</strong>, Maya <strong>carefully</strong> placed her bag <strong>outside</strong>.” <em>Yesterday</em> tells when, <em>carefully</em> tells how, and <em>outside</em> tells where.</p>
  </section>
</div>
